{"file":"Render-0.2.2-v2.zip","bytes":217164,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"render","description":"Deploy, debug, and monitor applications on Render. Includes skills, an agent, slash commands, a render.yaml validation hook, and the Render MCP server preconfigured over OAuth.","version":"0.2.2","license":"MIT","repository":"https://github.com/render-oss/render-plugin-claude-code","homepage":"https://github.com/render-oss/render-plugin-claude-code","keywords":["render","deploy","cloud","blueprint","monitoring","debugging"]}],"skills":[{"path":"skills/render-background-workers/SKILL.md","name":"render-background-workers","description":"Sets up and configures background workers on Render for queue-based job processing. Use when the user needs to process async jobs, consume from a queue, run Celery/Sidekiq/BullMQ/Asynq/Oban workers, handle graceful shutdown with SIGTERM, wire a worker to Key Value (Redis), or choose between workers and cron jobs for background work. Trigger terms: background worker, async jobs, queue consumer, Celery, Sidekiq, BullMQ, Asynq, Oban, job processing, SIGTERM, graceful shutdown.","headings":["Render Background Workers","When to Use","How Workers Work","Queue Framework Overview","Pairing with Key Value","Worker vs Cron vs Workflow","Graceful Shutdown","Blueprint Configuration","References","Related Skills"],"name_hint":"render · background · workers"},{"path":"skills/render-blueprints/SKILL.md","name":"render-blueprints","description":"Authors and validates render.yaml Blueprints for Render infrastructure. Use when the user needs to write or edit a render.yaml, wire services together with fromDatabase/fromService/fromGroup, set up projects and environments for multi-service apps, configure preview environments, validate against the schema, or fix immutable field errors. Trigger terms: render.yaml, Blueprint, IaC, fromDatabase, fromService, envVarGroups, previews, projects, environments.","headings":["Render Blueprints (render.yaml)","When to Use","Blueprint Structure","Top-level keys","Schema and IDE validation","Minimal example: web + PostgreSQL","Service Types","Runtimes","Cross-Service Wiring","`fromDatabase`","`fromService`","`fromGroup`","Other env var keys","Projects and Environments","Preview Environments","Validation","Immutable Fields","Services"],"name_hint":"render · blueprints"},{"path":"skills/render-cli/SKILL.md","name":"render-cli","description":"Installs and uses the Render CLI for deploys, logs, SSH, psql, Blueprint validation, and automation. Use when the user needs to run Render CLI commands, script deploys in CI/CD, authenticate with an API key, query services non-interactively, or troubleshoot CLI auth issues. Trigger terms: render CLI, render login, render deploys, render logs, render ssh, render psql, render blueprints validate, render skills, RENDER_API_KEY, non-interactive, CI/CD deploy.","headings":["Render CLI","When to Use","Installation","Authentication","Interactive (local dev)","Non-interactive (CI/CD)","Command Reference","Core commands","Non-interactive mode","Deploy patterns","Deploy and wait for completion (exits non-zero on failure)","Deploy a specific commit","Deploy a specific Docker image","Database queries","Single query, JSON output","CSV output via psql passthrough","CI/CD Example (GitHub Actions)","Local Config"],"name_hint":"render · cli"},{"path":"skills/render-cron-jobs/SKILL.md","name":"render-cron-jobs","description":"Configures and troubleshoots scheduled tasks on Render using cron job services. Use when the user needs to run something on a schedule, write a cron expression, set up a periodic job, migrate from Heroku Scheduler, choose between cron jobs and background workers, or fix a cron that isn''t firing. Trigger terms: cron job, scheduled task, periodic job, cron expression, schedule, run every, timer, Heroku Scheduler migration.","headings":["Render Cron Jobs","When to Use","Configuration","Constraints","Execution Behavior","Cron vs Worker vs Workflow","Blueprint Configuration","Common Patterns","References","Related Skills"],"name_hint":"render · cron · jobs"},{"path":"skills/render-debug/SKILL.md","name":"render-debug","description":"Debug failed Render deployments by analyzing logs, metrics, and database state. Identifies errors (missing env vars, port binding, OOM, etc.) and suggests fixes. Use when deployments fail, services won't start, or users mention errors, logs, or debugging.","headings":["Debug Render Deployments","When to Use This Skill","Prerequisites","MCP Setup","Debugging Workflow","Step 1: Identify Failed Service","Step 2: Retrieve Logs","Step 3: Analyze Error Patterns","Step 4: Check Metrics (Performance Issues)","Step 5: Debug Database Issues","Check database status","Check connections","Query directly","Step 6: Apply Fix","Step 7: Verify Fix","Check deploy status","Check for new errors","Check metrics"],"name_hint":"render · 排错"},{"path":"skills/render-deploy/SKILL.md","name":"render-deploy","description":"Deploy applications to Render by analyzing codebases, generating render.yaml Blueprints, and providing Dashboard deeplinks. Use when the user wants to deploy, host, publish, or set up their application on Render's cloud platform.","headings":["Deploy to Render","When to Use This Skill","Happy Path (New Users)","Choose Your Source Path","Choose Your Deployment Method (Git Repo)","Method Selection Heuristic","Prerequisites Check","Check if user is logged in (use -o json for non-interactive mode)","Method 1: Blueprint Deployment (Recommended for Complex Apps)","Blueprint Workflow","Step 1: Analyze Codebase","Step 2: Generate render.yaml","Step 2.5: Immediate Next Steps (Always Provide)","Step 3: Validate Configuration","Step 4: Commit and Push","Step 5: Generate Deeplink","Step 6: Guide User","Step 7: Verify Deployment"],"name_hint":"render · 部署"},{"path":"skills/render-disks/SKILL.md","name":"render-disks","description":"Attaches and manages persistent disks on Render services—mount paths, sizing, snapshots, file transfers, and single-instance constraints. Use when the user needs persistent storage, file uploads, a custom database on disk, CMS media storage, or needs to understand why their service can''t scale horizontally or use zero-downtime deploys. Trigger terms: persistent disk, disk, storage, mount path, sizeGB, SSD, file uploads, snapshots, disk restore, ephemeral filesystem.","headings":["Render Persistent Disks","When to Use","Critical Constraints","Setup","Dashboard","Blueprint","Mount Path","Disallowed mount paths","Snapshots","File Transfers","SCP (via SSH)","Download from service","Upload to service","Magic-Wormhole","On the service shell","On your local machine","Common Patterns","Common Mistakes"],"name_hint":"render · disks"},{"path":"skills/render-docker/SKILL.md","name":"render-docker","description":"Builds and deploys Docker containers on Render—Dockerfiles, multi-stage builds, Blueprint Docker fields, private registries, layer caching, and platform constraints. Use when the user mentions Docker, Dockerfile, container images, multi-stage builds, container registry, GHCR, ECR, BuildKit, dockerContext, runtime docker or image, or optimizing Docker builds on Render.","headings":["Render Docker Deployments","When to Use","Render Docker Builds","Blueprint Configuration","Multi-Stage Builds","Build Args vs Secrets","Registry Configuration","Layer Caching","Platform Specifics","`.dockerignore` and Start Commands","References","Related Skills"],"name_hint":"render · docker"},{"path":"skills/render-domains/SKILL.md","name":"render-domains","description":"Configures custom domains and TLS certificates on Render—DNS setup, CNAME records, apex domains, wildcard domains, and certificate troubleshooting. Use when the user needs to add a custom domain, configure DNS, set up HTTPS/TLS, troubleshoot certificate issuance, disable the onrender.com subdomain, or add a wildcard domain. Trigger terms: custom domain, DNS, CNAME, TLS, SSL, HTTPS, certificate, apex domain, wildcard domain, onrender.com, domain verification.","headings":["Render Custom Domains","When to Use","Domain Limits","Setup Steps","1. Add domain in Dashboard","2. Configure DNS","3. Verify domain","Wildcard Domains","CAA Records","Disabling the `onrender.com` Subdomain","Blueprint Configuration","Common Mistakes","References","Related Skills"],"name_hint":"render · domains"},{"path":"skills/render-env-vars/SKILL.md","name":"render-env-vars","description":"Configures environment variables, secrets, and env groups on Render. Use when the user needs to set env vars, wire secrets between services, create env groups, use generateValue, set sync: false, or troubleshoot missing or incorrect environment variable values in Blueprints or the Dashboard.","headings":["Environment Variables on Render","When to Use This Skill","Setting Variables","Dashboard","Blueprint (`render.yaml`)","MCP / API","Secret Management","Secret files","Environment Groups","Blueprint Wiring (Summary)","Platform-Injected Variables","Runtime-Specific Defaults","Common Issues","References","Related Skills"],"name_hint":"render · env · vars"},{"path":"skills/render-keyvalue/SKILL.md","name":"render-keyvalue","description":"Provisions and configures Render Key Value (Redis-compatible Valkey 8) instances for caching, session storage, and job queues. Use when the user needs Redis, Key Value, Valkey, a cache, session store, job queue backend, or needs to configure maxmemory policy, ipAllowList, connection strings, or internal vs external access. Trigger terms: Key Value, Redis, Valkey, cache, session store, REDIS_URL, maxmemory, ipAllowList, allkeys-lru, noeviction.","headings":["Render Key Value","When to Use","Key Concepts","Valkey 8 (not Redis)","Connection URLs","Internal authentication","Maxmemory Policy","Blueprint Configuration","`ipAllowList` is required","Wiring to services","Data Persistence","Instance Types and Upgrades","Connection Exam